{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>El</b> — like לא (negative particle). Thus the form of the negative: אל מות בסודם (Psalm 26:9), אל תבא נפשי (Psalm 26:9). The psalmist says to his soul, or to the exiles: if your help is from HaShem alone, do not fear, for He will not let your foot slip when you walk in the city streets, or on the wall." "<b>And your keeper will not slumber</b> — for every city that is under siege has guards on the walls at night."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 121, :notes {0 "Resolved אל as the negative particle לא throughout; the phrase 'דרך נתינה' (manner of negation) introduces the grammatical point."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:09.175029011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}